From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: John Rowley <johnrowleyster@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 01:48:58 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] feat(miniwin): draw viewports into their rectangles and clear
 on request

CreateViewport's x and y now place the viewport: GetX and GetY return
them, and the renderer gets a viewport rectangle (SetViewportRect,
default ignored) that the viewport's projection is centred on and that
its drawing is clipped to. A viewport re-applies its rectangle,
projection and frustum on every Render and when it becomes the device's
current viewport, so two viewports on one device no longer share the
last one's projection. The frustum planes are derived from the
projection, so they hold for any front plane.

IDirect3DViewport3::Clear2 and Viewport::Clear(flags) clear rectangles,
clipped to the viewport, of the target (to a colour, or to the scene's
background) and the z-buffer, through a new renderer entry point,
ClearRect. Its default clears only the whole target. Viewport::Clear()
clears both, as D3DRM does.

The software backend implements both. Once the client clears the
z-buffer itself, BeginFrame stops clearing it, so drawing can continue
across Render calls until the next clear; LEGO Island, which never
clears z, keeps the per-frame clear.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

